ly CA file to trust, or #f for the system") (107 "                      store; #f. A path beginning pkcs11:, in any") (108 "                      ASCII case, is refused: reach such a file as") (109 "                      ./pkcs11:... On any Guix libcurl, a submit") (110 "                      refuses a CA file, verify on, when SSL_CERT_FILE") (111 "                      or SSL_CERT_DIR was set at the load, which") (112 "                      would replace it, or add to it; and on macOS") (113 "                      with Apple's LibreSSL in use, which checks the") (114 "                      keychain when it fails: set") (115 "                      CURL_SSL_BACKEND=secure-transport") (116 "  verify              whether to verify the peer; #t") (117 "  proxy               environment, through the proxy http_proxy,") (118 "                      https_proxy or all_proxy names, by libcurl's") (119 "                      rules; #f, direct; or a URL string, an http:// or") (120 "                      https:// proxy every transfer goes through,") (121 "                      whatever a variable says, no_proxy among them,") (122 "                      its userinfo the proxy's credentials, sent by") (123 "                      Basic, a URL with no port given its scheme's;") (124 "                      environment. A submit refuses a URL that does not") (125 "                      parse (proxy-url), a scheme but http or https") (126 "                      (proxy-scheme), a path, a query or a fragment") (127 "                      (proxy-url-parts), and userinfo that decodes to a") (128 "                      control byte, to bytes that are not UTF-8, or to") (129 "                      a colon in the user (credentials-bytes), or to") (130 "                      nothing (credentials-empty), naming the field,") (131 "                      never the URL") (132 "  stream-buffer       the bytes of the response's body the token") (133 "                      buffers, a positive exact integer, read as it") (134 "                      arrives through the token; or #f, the whole body") (135 "                      in the response; #f. Refused beside an Expect") (136 "                      header whose value holds 100-continue, as") (137 "                      stream-with-rounds") (138 "  body-length         a streamed body's length, an exact natural below") (139 "                      2^63 - 1, sent as Content-Length; or #f, chunked") (140 "                      over HTTP/1.1; #f. Refused beside a body that does") (141 "                      not stream, as body-length-without-stream") (142 "  http-version        http/1.1; http/2, by ALPN over https://, HTTP/1.1") (143 "                      over http://; http/2-prior-knowledge, HTTP/2 with") (144 "                      no HTTP/1.1 first, for http:// alone: a submit") (145 "                      refuses it with an https:// URL, as") (146 "                      prior-knowledge-over-https; or #f, libcurl's own,") (147 "                      which acts as http/2; #f. Requests started") (148 "                      together open their own connections, but for two") (149 "                      by prior knowledge on 7.85.0, which share one; a") (150 "                      later one reuses an open one: over http://, a #f") (151 "                      or http/2 request to an origin the engine holds") (152 "                      an HTTP/2 connection to, made by prior knowledge,") (153 "                      reuses it and reads HTTP/2") (154 "  credentials         a server's credentials, one scheme's, each part a") (155 "                      string sent as UTF-8: (basic USER PASSWORD) and") (156 "                      (bearer TOKEN), sent on the first request; (digest") (157 "                      USER PASSWORD), sent once the server challenges a") (158 "                      bare first request, so a request with a body to a") (159 "                      server that never does goes twice, the first with") (160